Let a layer name the app and the profiles it carries: TOLKARA_DISPLAY_NAME, TOLKARA_PROFILES, layer.env.

Brighter Pocket's build of Tolkara should read "Brighter Pocket" on the Home Screen and carry
only the Brighter Shores profile: the platform's others (WoW, Cyberpunk 2077, Heroes III)
are neither built nor tested with this layer and must not appear in its library. Both are
now settings, with the platform's behaviour as their defaults:
- TOLKARA_DISPLAY_NAME (tools/generate.sh, default Tolkara) is the Tolkara target's
  CFBundleDisplayName, and tools/package_ipa.sh's name for the unsigned .ipa.
- TOLKARA_PROFILES, folder names under profiles/ separated by ':', limits the profiles
  tools/build_emulated_guest.sh puts in the app (empty: all of them, as before).
- tools/localenv.sh and tools/localenv.py read layer.env, committed defaults a layer ships
  (Brighter Pocket's is pocket/layer.env, an overlay file), before local.env; local.env and
  the environment still win. Without layer.env nothing changes.
Upstream candidate: brand-free, and the platform's own builds come out as before.

--- a/tools/localenv.sh
+++ b/tools/localenv.sh
@@ -1,11 +1,14 @@
 # Sourced by the shell tools: read the ignored local.env (KEY=value lines).
 # Settings already in the environment win, as in tools/localenv.py, so
 # `TOLKARA_MODE=local-signing tools/run.sh sim` works with any local.env.
+# A layer built on Tolkara may ship layer.env, committed defaults for its
+# builds (an app name, say), read first: local.env and the environment win.
 tolkara_load_env() {
     local given
     # Re-export: 'declare -x', as bash lists it, would be local to this function.
     # POSIX mode lists 'export NAME=' instead; accept both.
     given=$(export -p | sed -n -E 's/^(declare -x|export) ((DEVELOPMENT_TEAM|TOLKARA_[A-Z_]+|DEVICE|SIMULATOR|GUEST_EXE|NATIVE_GUEST_SHIMS|SIGN_IDENTITY)=)/export \2/p')
+    if [ -f layer.env ]; then set -a; . ./layer.env; set +a; fi
     if [ -f local.env ]; then set -a; . ./local.env; set +a; fi
     eval "$given"
 }
